  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Various other social games have NSFW DLC in one form or another, preventing minors from seeing NSFW content while opening the game for others.\nA one-off payment of just $5-10 (along with some form of age-verification) would act as a firm barrier against most children being exposed to NSFW content in worlds.\nThis cost would also be low enough that most adults could afford, and would help support the continued development of VRChat.\nMy suggestion is to loosen the restrictions on NSFW content in public worlds, but to increase the penalty for not properly tagging avatars and worlds.\nThen, allow NSFW content to be public, but hidden by default unless the player allows the content to be viewed, and/or has the DLC for higher levels of NSFW\n(i.e: gore would be hidden but showable without DLC, but nudity would require the DLC)\nWhile this is a suggestion for the devs, I would also like to hear what the community thinks about this request. Please leave your comments and ideas below. :3\nLet's make VRChat a community that's safter for children, and better for everyone.",
